cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite both the software archive and the accompanying paper."
title: "HİP: a privacy-preserving, unique-code-based mobile application for asynchronous multi-physician clinical data collection"
abstract: >-
  A cross-platform mobile application in which several physicians contribute
  structured clinical data for one patient under a shared 20-character code,
  each within their own specialty category and asynchronously. The system
  tracks which contributions remain pending and exports the consolidated
  record as a spreadsheet matching the input schema of the decision support
  system it serves. Authorisation is enforced server-side by versioned,
  deny-by-default Firestore security rules.
